Spectacular rendition on space station
Astronaut Scott Parazynski and his crew comrade of the International Space Station (ISS) will have needed more than seven hours of work in space to carry out the spectacular repair of a torn and indispensable solar panel for the continuation of the station's scientific activities.
A risky exit that accumulated the records because of its duration, its departure from the habitable modules, of the speed with which it has been imagined has been imagined, astronaut astronauts to carry out the repair.
Troubles appeared on Tuesday that astronauts had released the Harmony module from the Discovery shuttle, a cylindrical cooling-clad piece commissioned to soon host European and Japanese scientific laundries (seen).
This la module is a type of landing platform for lab-modities.
But we must be able to provide them in electricity.
The second task of the crew was therefore to displace an electricity production module with solar panels that weighed 17.5 tons, already present on the ISS, in order to put it in its final position.
After having displaced him, the crew began the reorganization of the solar panels of the module that are 76 meters sized.
And that's where one of the panels, which unveils as accordions, has been damaged in just about a metre by a cable that was stuck.
The roll-out has been stopped so as not to damage the panel anymore.
The astronauts, who at the beginning had to carry out a Discovery shuttle's control outlet, and then go to repair another solar panel whose rotrotating system was defective, were forced to dedicate themselves to the damaged panel.
And it's Scott Parazynski who's been picked to snail at the end of the 30-met metre-long shuttle-in-arm arm added to the station to make the repair.
It's one of Nasa's best "spacewalker."
Tall, rugged, very skilful, he's got a very developed torso and long arms.
At the age of 46, this training doctor has been in charge of "operating" the "wounded" solar panel.
After precisely inspecting the damage, he severed the fallible cable and installed types of "tablillas" in the damaged area.
He had been aided by the second "spacewalker" that had stayed near the air lock and, from the inside, by other astronauts such as Peggy Whitson, the crew commander.
The tool he used, a hockey mini blazer wrapped with insulator to prevent electrocution on solar panels that produced several hundreds of volts, has been concoctuated and "puzzled" by astronauts aboard the station.
Upon completion of the operation, Scott Parazynski waited for the panel to be fully deployed before making the inventory of its instruments and returning inside the station.
Yesterday in the afternoon, astronauts took advantage of a no-day rest before seven astronauts returned from the Discovery shuttle for the return to Earth planned on Wednesday.
The EADS title sanctioned on the stock exchange
The EADS stock is currently downgraded to the Paris Stock Exchange, after the aeronautics and defence group has announced that it will have to spend between 1.2 and 1.4bn euros to deal with A400M delays.
EADS loses 4 per cent to EUR 21.96 currently to the Paris Stock Exchange.
The group has been obliged to review its forecast of the operational outcome for 2007 in response to delays spawned by the slow progression of engine development of the A400M engine, which is conditioning the plane's inaugural flight.
The cost of alleviating the delay taken in the delivery of the military transport plane, announced in October, amounts "between 1.2 to 1.4 billion euros, of which more than 1 billion for Airbus ," announced the mother house of European builder EADS.
Due to these loads, EADS will be forced to announce new objectives of the operating result (EBIT) for 2007 during the presentation of its quarterly results next Thursday, it adds without any more encrypted precision.
The group also indicates that the estimation of the new charges is consistent with the six-month delay.
It should be remembered that EADS' operational result failed from 86 per cent in 2006, mainly because of loads linked to the delays of another programme, that of the very thick A380 carrier.
The group initially envoked a first installment of the A400M to the French army in October 2009.
Choosing the status quo
Neither surprise on Sunday, at the exit of the polls: the Russians are going to mass-choppose for President Poutine's party, united Russia.
Confirming his aspiration for stability, including authoritarianism, after a very limited campaign.
Three days after the legislative elections, Russian President Vladimir Putin sends a televised message to the voters today about public channels, already registered but whose content is kept secret.
He does so as leader of the list for united Russia, the pro-Kremlin party whose victory proves crushing.
Yesterday, the president didn't make it easy to receive the foreign ambassadors, content himself with handing over a new charge against the West accused of interfering - his predilection theme during the campaign.
"We know the price of a true democracy and we want honest, more transparent and more open elections, elections without incidents," he added.
According to the opposition, we are a long way from the truth.
He denounces a campaign tarnished because of pressure.
Communist Leader Guennadi Ziouganov says there is "never having such dirty choices, until the time of Eltsin."
Following last weekend's crackdown on rallies of rallies, former jacket world champion Garry Kasparov, sentenced to five days in prison for an illegal demonstration, visits are prohibited according to his lawyer.
"The Russians guarded the mentality of the Soviet homo".
Behind these unsurprising legislative elections two much more open questions emerge:
Who's gonna succeed Poutine for the presidency?
The official newspaper yesterday published the date of the first round of the presidential election on 2 March 2008; the candidates have until December 23 to make themselves known.
Elected in 2000 and re-elected in 2004, Vladimir Putin is unable to apply for the third consecutive term.
Then no successor emerges.
What role will Poutine play after March?
- Prime Minister?
The boss of the Parliamentary Majority and the very mighty united Russia party elected by the government and the president?
Either it is to the legislative elections such as the presidential elections, the out-of-empt power will triumph.
It's a tradition.
"The Russians retained the mentality of homo sovieticus, they don't own their destiny ," says sociologist Lev Goudkov, director of the Levada independent center.
The historian Nikola Kopossov, of St.Petersburg State University, dates back further: civil society lagged behind in this Christianized country five centuries after Europe; the famous spirit of the community delayed the formation of individualism.
After the liberal reforms of the 1990s, "Poutine re-established the model of a paternalistic state, perfectly accepted by the population since this new paternalism has not been followed by terrorism, but by a certain economic relief ," says Maria Lipman of the Carnegie Foundation.
Today the Russians "reject of their own volition of the personal responsibility" of those who had briefly hinted after the outbreak of the USSR.
"Why what to reflect?"
Footage touches all social strata, including the world of affairs.
And the administrative elite plans to preserve the status quo: 65 governors (out of every 85 heads of Russian regions) run local lists of united Russia..
New freedoms imported from the West are often synonymous with chaos, such as in the 1990s.
Opinion prefers stability.
On behalf that the Russians won't vote for the extremists either.
Conclusion by Tamara Tcherednitchenko, a 54-year-old professor: "Why what to reflect?
Those in power aren't too bad, why change them?"
Heavy Memory
After more than 60 years of a confidential nature, Bad Arolsen &apos; s Nazi archives, describing the fates of 17.5 million victims of the Hitler regime, are freely accessible.
The 47 million archival documents, stored about 27 km of shelves to Bad Arolsen (Hesse), were not so far complimentable only in a "humanitarian" purpose, i.e. individually and nominative, at the request of an old victim or their beneficiaries.
The eleven managing states - such as Germany, France, Israel and the U.S. - reached an agreement in May 2006 to open them to search engines and historians.
Since the process of ratification of this agreement by all States has been completed, the aperture has become effective since yesterday.
Sensitive information
historians' access to Bad Arolsen will make it possible to make searches "in particular on the movements of prisoners, the population of the camps and the state of health of forced workers ," explains Reto Meistern, the director of these archives administered by the International Commission of the Red Cross (ICRC).
Until recently, a number of states, such as Germany, were opposed to the public's accommodation of these nominating documents, due to the sensitive nature of certain information.
As well as alleged homosexuality or the mental hándicap of certain decommissioning victims.
The records of the concentration camps or detention orders established by the Gestapo had been assembled after the war for a practical purpose: to find countrymen deported or subjected in compulsory work and, eventually, to provide them with proof of their internment, in order to open the way to their compensation.
Already today in Bad Arolsen, more than 300 permanent wage earners are dealing with tens of thousands of individual requests.
However, for a part of the scientific community, access to Bad Arolsen is of limited interest.
"There is nothing fundamentally new to expect from these documents," said Professor Wolfgang Benz, director of the Search Centre on anti-Semitism at the Technische Universitat in Berlin in 2006.
The European Union and India want to reach a free-for-trade agreement in 2008
At the same time, Indo-European bilateral trade already reaches about EUR 60 billion a year.
The European Union is India &apos; s first trading partner and accounts for 18 per cent of its foreign trade.
The European Union and India are hoping to sign a free-for-trade agreement in 2008, said European Trade commissioner Peter Mandelson and his Indian counterpart Kamal Nath.
The foreign ministers of the European Union had given their approval to the European Commission last April to begin negotiations aimed to sign free trade agreements (ALE) with India, South Korea and the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (Asean). Indo-European bilateral trade already reaches about 60 billion euros a year.
The European Union is India &apos; s first trading partner and accounts for 18 per cent of its foreign trade.
LUE is also its first foreign investor, but India is only the 9th trading partner of the European Union, according to figures from the European Commission.
"A free-chandise pact will badly frighten both economies" and "India would improve its entry into a market of 450 million prosperous Europeans," said Peter Mandelson.
Europe represents the first or the second market for each of the top ten products exported by India, the European commissioner said. The Asian and European giants change annually to "47 billion euros of goods " and for " ten billion euros of services ," said this this week Dani?le Smadja, head of the European Commission delegation in New Delhi, feeling that bilateral trade "has not yet reached its potential." The European Union and India meet on Friday for their eighth diplomatic summit in New Delhi in the presence of Prime Minister Manmohan Singh and in the presence of European Commission President José Manuel Durao Barroso.
(Source AFP)
The Bank of England takes note of worries by offering . . . . . . . . . . . . .
The Bank of England on Thursday was eager to ease the current turnaround of concerns about credit conditions, and announced an offer of 10 billion pound pounds to the 5.75 per cent base index in five weeks, an offer of an unus-usual duration.
"In order to alleviate the concerns that financial market conditions will be particularly tight at the end of the year, and to give the banks a greater certainty in the way in which they organise their liquidity positions over this period, the Bank intends to offer a significant proportion of its planned reserve contribution during the maintenance period beginning on 6 December in the form of a five-week open market operation," he said in a statement.
The bank says 10 billion pounds (EUR 14 billion) will be put on the market on December 6 at 12pm 15 GMT, the base index until January 10.
It's the first time it looks like the England BoE bank has been on the market for five weeks in an open-market operation.
These are usually done within a week.
The BoE adds in its statement that it "was prepared to take other steps to maintain indexes" of inter-bank loans a day in line with its core index.
Wednesday's Inter-Bank Index was 5,829.
The after-three-month index was set at 6.6 percent, the highest since Sept.
From the beginning of the financial crisis of the summer, the sums placed on the market by the Bank of England were combined with a significant penalty rate that had deterred banks from resorting to that.
According to some rumours, corroborated by the evolution of the change in the pound relative to the euro, many had preferred to underwrite the sums brought to the market by the European Central Bank, the most advantageous indices and with more assured discretion.
The UMP and NC parties deny consideration of the PS party's proposals on purchasing power
The UMP and Nouveau Centre group on Thursday refused to discuss articles of the socialist proposition on purchasing power, which amounts to a dismissal of the text.
Based on a socialist "niche" (assion for the initiative of a Parliamentary Group), the text declined a dozen measures taken on Tuesday by the PS's national office, among which an increase of 50 per cent in the bonus for employment, the re-establishment of TIPP (indominant rate per oil products) floating, a check-transport or rental restrictions.
Since the UMP and NC have voted against the examination of the articles (180 voices against 115), the session has been adjourned at the end of the general discussion that gave rise to exchanges, sometimes alive, between a majority and opponent a few hours of Nicolas Sarkozy's televised intervention on purchasing power.
PS deputy leader Jean Marc Ayrault has announced that his group would represent the integrity of its proposals in the form of amendments to the Amending Finance Bill reviewed by the Asemblea next week.
A new festival comes to light
As a result of numerous rumbling rumours regarding the creation by C3 Presents of a new music festival in Philadelphia, the promoter/producer announces the Vineland Music Festival in New Jersey, in collaboration with Festival Republic by British producer Melvin Benn.
"For our company, it's an honor to work with a person who inspired, no more or less, the current movement of festivals in America ," Charlie Jones of C3 confided at Billboard.com.
C3 produces the Lollapalooza festival in Chicago and the Austin City Limits Music Festival.
Vineland in New Jersey is a summer destination for the campsite.
The festival would take place August 8-10 on a 500-a-a-a-acre private farm about 40 minutes from Philadelphia.
Once known as Mean Fiddler, Festival Republic director Melvin Benn is one of the world's most respected festival producers.
In 1989, he took the direction of the Reading Festival in the United Kingdom, which attracts some 80,000 people annually.
In 1999, Melvin Benn Added the Leeds Festival to his portfolio later, in 2006, the Festival Republic created the Henham Park Latitude Festival in the Suffolk.
Since 2002, as a co-owner, Melvin Benn has also been in charge of the production, licensing and organizational tasks of the Glastonbury Festival, which can now accommodate up to 177 500 people.
Qualifying Glastonbury as "most inspiring event" I've ever attended, Charlie Jones of C3 says his company and Melvin Benn's are working in parallel to give the region a European-style festival-event.
"We'd chosen Philadelphia as a crook and worked perseveringly with the Fairmount Parks Commission to create a festival in downtown Philadelphia ," says Charlie Jones.
"We were in negotiations with the city and the Commission was motivated and enthusiastic about this project.
"Unfortunately we stagnate into low-level policies because of the current administration," Charlie Jones said.
" Fortunately, we were able to argue with Melvin Benn and we are preparing to create a magnificent festival in an exceptional place that, lately, will take place in Philadelphia."
C3 Presents resurrected the Lollapalooza festival in 2005 at Chicago's Grant Park, after detaching itself in the festival landscape in 2002 with the Austin City Limits Music Festival.
Both events accounted for gross revenues of $9.81m and $11.3 billion in 2007.
These two festivals take place in an urban environment.
"Melvin Benn's European model is a country festival, while ours are done rather in urban green areas," says Charlie Jones.
The objective is to merge, in one way or the other, both formulas in order to give at the same time an impression of a country festival in the European and urban way in an American way."
Vineland is roughly halfway between Philadelphia and Atlantic City.
"Vineland community, including the mayor, enthusiast enthusiastically supports celebrating this event," says Charlie Jones.
The latter refuses to unveil the terms of the agreement, but states: "They are quite interesting to allow you to invest in such an event and host a festival that, we hope, will have a long life."
Charlie Jones says this festival's hotel offer is "very large," an example of that of 80,000 people at the Bonnaroo Music Festival in the Tennessee.
He says that invitations have been thrown to the groups, but that nothing could yet be confirmed at the time of going under the press.
"Vineland will have the flavour of rock, but the music will be varied there, in the hope of attracting all kinds of spectators," says Charlie Jones.
His classmates from C3, who received the Top Independent Promoter award for the latest Billboard Touring Awards, are Charlie Walker and Charles Attal.:
