Will there be end-of-the-year rallies on the stock exchange? The experts, divided by the 'subprime' crisis.
Less than a five-week bid to fare from the end of the financial year, investors are already rubbing their hands expecting the traditional end-of-year rally to arrive.
However, this year the pundits aren't so clear that it's going to happen.
Banif believes that "from a statistic point of view, the month of December on the stock exchange usually has a positive behavior.
However, it is not appropriate to make forecasts solely on the basis of the statistics, even more so because in the current context the uncertainties lurk on the markets, at least in the short term."
Although they are not in favour of the fringing stock market in the last few weeks of the year, these experts point out that "the stock market is supported by the existence of liquidity, willing to invest given the lack of alternatives with guarantees, especially fixed income, affected by the flight effect towards quality values both in the long and short sections."
For this reason, they believe that the stock exchange will have a rather lateral behavior, not without volatility "especially because it is not known the impact of the likely decline of the Fed's rates, given the high level of crude oil and the danger of stimulating inflationary tensions."
Javier Barrio, BPI sales manager in Spain, agrees that it is not a good time to venture to say that there is going to be a rally.
"It's not the thing for a lot of cheers," the expert says.
The Ibex has lost about 4 per cent since peaks on November 8, when the index closed at 15,945.7 points.
Still, not all the experts have such a negative vision.
Juan Solana, analyst at Intermoney, believes that the Ibex 35 could close the year closer to 16,000 points thanks to the restructuring of the portfolios and the traditional contributions to the pension plans that occur every year on these dates.
However, the expert qualifies that things will be somewhat different this year as he believes that the rally will advance to the second week of December, after the bridge of the Constitution.
Analyst doesn't think the volatility is going to affect market trends.
Federico Olucha, an analyst at Inversis Banco, estimates that we are close to technical levels and "we could therefore be able to see a bounce from the index that could be boosted depending on news coming from the U.S. regarding the consequences of the crisis in the credit market."
Analysts are confident they'll be positive.
Analysts agree when it comes to choosing the values that will be in charge of taking the Ibex towards new maximum levels.
Solana of Intermoney states that "this year it is up to the great values."
The expert would include in the portfolio the two big banks and some builders "because when the date arrives, the electricity sector will be very expensive."
Meanwhile, Federico Olucha of Inversis Banco assures that the rises will come from the hand of banking and the industrial sector.
Builsurers will also be able to benefit from this rally, if it occurs.
"ACS has been recovering positions for several months and we hope that other construction companies such as Ferrovial and FCC will go the same way," the expert explains.
Cyclic consumption will be the protagonist in the latter part of the year due to the increase in sales in the Christmas sales season.
On the other hand, the expert believes that technologies will also do very well although in this case there is not much representation in the Spanish market.
Five-something in seven years
In the last seven years, on only two occasions December it has been a bassy month.
The real end-of-a-year rally took place in 2003, when the stock markets emerged from the crisis caused by the puncture of the tech bubble.
This year, in which the Ibex 35 regained 28.17%, December recorded a rebound of 6.68 per cent.
We will have to see if 2007 is the fifth consecutive year of profits (for the moment the Ibex rises by 8.36% from January) and whether it manages to count on its end-of-the-year rally.
Popular will open 200 offices 12 p.m. from Monday to Saturday
Popular has decided to renovate much of its offices.
In a total of 200, those located in the most commercial areas of Spain.
These branches, which will operate under the Popular Max brand, represent a big change for the bank.
Also for the rest of the Spanish entities, since it is the first group that decides to make the leap to bet on the uninterrupted inauguration of their agencies until 8.30 p.m., and open on Saturdays from 10 a.m. to 8.30 p.m.
Another group that has also reiterated on a number of occasions that it wanted to extend the schedules of its branches, BBVA, has not yet decided to take the step.
Meanwhile, it is about to close an agreement with the unions to close 75% of their offices on Saturdays in exchange for opening an afternoon, although not to the public.
The results of Popular &apos; s experience will be decisive for other entities to take aim or not at this initiative that supports the schedules of the shops.
Precisely this is the objective that Popular pursues with the project.
Recreate the private customers who move through these areas to make their purchases, to SMEs, self-employed people and shops of the streets chosen to open.
The bank wants to have these 200 offices open throughout Spain in about 18 months, since they are not new openings but remodeling of existing ones.
To this end, the entity will modernize the branches that it already has in commercial areas, adapting them to the profile presented by the customers of the different streets.
In this way, the extension of the schedules is accompanied by a different conception of the space of the branch and a new design, more current, with brighter colors.
The head of commercial banking, Ángel Rivera, assures that this restructuring does not represent a great investment, although a greater recruitment of personnel, since it goes from having about six employees per premises to eight or nine.
The offices, which will even have spaces for SMEs to be able to assemble there, will sell non-Financial products.
A positive experience for the group
Popular has already tested its initiative in three offices in Madrid.
And the experience has been positive, as explained by Ángel Rivero.
The branches of Bravo Murillo, O'Donnell and Gran Via de Madrid streets have been chosen, and it seems that it is successful, according to Rivero.
Popular currently has 2,500 branches.
And another 60 that operate under the Mundocredit brand, specializing in immigrants, also with very spacious schedules, that even open on Sundays and holidays.
In these PopularMax premises they will not repeat the BBVA model, where several of their offices have a wide range of non-financial products for sale.
'We don't wanna compete with our customers,' says Rivero.
For the moment, they have reached an agreement with Telefónica to sell mobile phones, with personnel outside the bank.
Telecinco dwindles for the first time the stock market value of its rival Antena 3
We've made it.'
Yesterday Paolo Vasile, CEO of Telecinco expressed his satisfaction at the close of the market, when he noted that the chain he directed doubled the value of its rival, Antena 3.
Only one aspect tarnished his joy: 'It's what hurts me, it's not 'cause we've grown more but because we've come down less,' he said.
Even so, he emphasized that in a weak market, 'we have fallen less.'
Telecinco ended the day yesterday with an advance of 2.54%.
That gain puts its loss so far this year at 15.56 per cent.
The stock exchange value of the company controlled by Mediaset (with 52% of the capital) and owned by Vocento (another 13%) thus reaches 4,488.88 million euros, according to Bloomberg's data.
Its rival Antena 3, which yesterday yielded 1.52% and accumulates a decrease of 40.5 per cent since January, halves EUR 2,193.46 million.
The value of the other quoted communication companies amounts to 3,571 million for Sogecable; 2,518.53 million Prisa (editor of Cinco Días) and 1,779 million Vocent.
According to Vasile, the comparison with Antena 3 is because 'we're talking about two similar companies.
The relative fact is how much we'll be able to do, in the same market, at what cost and how we rent it in terms of the audience.'
Telecinco announced last this week that it plans to become the first television network this year to exceed 1 billion gross advertising revenue, according to Giuseppe Tringali, the CEO of Telecinco and Publiespaña, the subsidiary that manages the advertising of the group.
If this advertised data became real, the television network would record an increase of 3.6% in its advertising turnover compared to 965,4 million in the financial year 2006.
For its part, Antena 3's net turnover increased by 1.6% in the first nine months of the financial year (until 734,4 million) while net television revenues grew by 0.7 per cent ($630.4 million).
One of the factors indicated by analysts for the best relative evolution on the Telecinco Stock Exchange is the high pay out it has maintained so far: in 2006, the company chaired by Alejandro Echevarría distributed 100% of the profit among its shareholders.
Vasile assures that, although it is too early to make the decision, this ratio could vary after buying 33% of Endemol in association with its Mediaset matrix.
'We have an official commitment to give at least 50 per cent, although we've always declared a lot more.
This year, I hope that we will be able to leave happy our shareholders, to whom we have already valued 33 per cent of Endemol.
According to analysts, the market at the same time shows some tiredness.
Lehman Brothers recently downgraded Telecinco's profit estimates by 4 per cent and in 2009, 7 per cent.
It is due, they explain, to having cut the projected income growth from 10.5 per cent to 8.4 per cent in 2008 and from 5.5 per cent to 5.1 per cent in 2009.
This same firm has lowered Antena &apos; s profit forecast by 3.4 per 4.5 per cent in 2008 and 7.5 per cent in 2009.
3 views
1.
Ibersecurities: it recommends buying both securities based mainly on their high dividend and long-lasting sustainable profitability.
2.
Caja Madrid: sees Telecinco (accumulating) better than Antena 3 (keep) for the 'attractive multiples' and rise of the business.
3.
JPMorgan: It recommends under-estimating in both cases by having 'similar threats' (saturated market and poorer economic climate).
The Congress approves the transposition of the Mifid, which came into force 1 November
Parallel to its parliamentary process, which ended today with a vote by Congress on the amendments incorporated into the bill in the Senate, the Government has submitted to a public hearing the regulations that will carry out the new law, with the aim of both coming into force before the end of the year.
The representatives of the different groups agreed to highlight the efforts made by deputies and senators to negotiate and agree on the best regulation in order to ensure the protection of investors and to regulate in detail the activities of the entities so that the markets operate efficiently.
Mifid, which amends the Law on the Stock Market, implies the modernization of financial markets, while strengthening investor protection, improves the supervisory powers of the National Securities Market Commission (CNMV) and fosters cooperation between the different supervisors of the European Union.
The new regulations will make it possible to provide financial advisory services to both specialized firms and natural or legal persons and creates a new type of financial services firm (ESIS), financial advisory firms (AFIs), which are linked to securities companies, equity agencies and holding- managing companies.
In addition, it expands the number of systems for the implementation of transactions on financial instruments, so that regulated secondary markets are joined by multilateral negotiating systems and order internalization systems, which will compete with current stock exchange managers.
The Act also obliges investment service companies to disclose in the market information about the key aspects of their business profile, exposure to risk and forms of risk management and requires them to keep a record of all the operations they carry out, in order to facilitate supervision by the CNMV.
In his passage through the Economics Committee of Congress, several modifications were incorporated, among which he emphasizes that secupied debts are regarded as a "complex" financial instrument given its high danger to the investor, which has been demonstrated by what has happened with the debt of high-risk U.S. (subprime).
In addition, it took advantage of the transposition of the directive in order to legally delineate the functions that can be carried out by graduate graduates in Economics and Entrepreneurs 30 years after the approval in 1977 of the royal decree delimiting the professional functions reserved for economists.
For its part, the Senate incorporated the creation of new figures in the financial sector, such as that of the mediator, who will work as an employee, will not require the authorization of the CNMV and will be able to provide its services for the commercialization of products and the recruitment of clients to different investment companies at the same time.
Harmonised CPI rises five-tenths in November to 4.1 per cent
This indicator, which then serves Eurostat to incorporate it to the calculation of the inflation rate in the European Union, provides an advance on how prices in Spain evolved during the month of November.
Its publication responds to the policy of Eurostat and the European Central Bank (ECB) to provide data comparable in time and quality to those produced in the United States.
The advance indicator is calculated using the same procedure as that used for the Harmonized Consumer Price Indice, but using various statistical modelling methods to estimate the information that is not yet available at the time of its publication.
The INE recalled that the information provided by the advance indicator is only indicative, so it does not necessarily have to coincide with the definitive data, which will be released on December 14.
"The CPI will continue at relatively high levels"
The second vice-president and Minister of the Economy, Pedro Solbes, has stated that the 4.1% increase in the CPI in November is a "temporary encryption," but at the same time has predicted that the price index will continue at "relatively high" levels in the coming months.
In any case Solbes has pointed out in the corridors of Congress that "although the figure isn't good" Spain's inflation differential with respect to the monetary union remains "more or less" the same in recent years.
He has also explained that in November "there has been less surprise" than in the previous month, when the government did not have such a high increase.
"We were expecting a figure of around 4%," the Minister of the Economy acknowledged regarding the data advanced today.
Virgin is planning to raise with Northern Rock $42 billion over three years
Northern Rock deposits have fallen by more than 50 per cent to 12 billion pounds ($16.8bn euros) since it entered crisis in mid-September and had to rely on an emergency loan from the Bank of England.
At that time he amassed record deposits of more than 25 billion pounds, a figure that has progressively fallen in two and a half months due to the mistrust of his clients and despite the 100 per cent guarantee of the money offered by the Government and maintained until the end of the crisis.
Virgin, which would rebrand the entity with its financial trademark Virgin Money, needs to capture around a quarter of the revenue at British banks deposited over the next three years to get that remaining 18 billion pounds to the target of $30 billion.
Gov. Richard Branson's group, known for its eye-catching advertising campaigns in the United Kingdom, intends to spend 50 million pounds (about 70 million euros) a year on advertising and marketing to achieve its purpose.
Northern Rock this week named Virgin's consortium's offer, which includes three other companies as its favourite to rescue it from bankruptcy.
Totana Mayor Arrested for Alleged plot of urban corruption
The Civil Guard arrested today early in the morning the current mayor of the Murcian municipality of Totana (of the Popular Party) for his alleged relationship with the plot of urban corruption uncovered this week.
In addition, one of the secretaries of the consistory and the police chief of the municipality have also been arrested.
José Martínez Andreo replaced last May Juan Morales, the current popular congresswoman, and until then governor of the municipality, who according to sources of the investigation consulted by Cadena SER, could be the 'cabecilla' of this plot.
The agents continue to register the municipal units and the Urban Planning Council and no further arrests are ruled out in the next few hours.
In addition, Juan Morales &apos; s lawyer, the main suspect in the plot of urban corruption unveiled earlier this week, has been charged.
As the SER Caden was reported yesterday to the lawyer of the 'popular' deputy Juan Morales, he was therefore arrested leaving Morales's home with important documentation related to the plot.
Moreover, the purpose of the investigation, according to sources of the investigation, is the alleged collection of Morales commissions in exchange for facilitating the signing of an urban agreement with a Galician construction company to reclassify 200 hectares of land.
At the moment there are eight people in custody.
Bono agrees to lead PSOE Candidacy for Toledo and preside over Congress if they win
The former Minister of Defense José Bono has accepted the offer of the president of the government and secretary general of the socialists, José Luis Rodríguez Zapatero, to top the PSOE list by Toledo for the next general elections and be president of the Congress in the event that the socialists win the general elections.
This was announced at a press conference by the Secretary of Organization of the PSOE, José Blanco, and Bono himself, after the meeting he held this noon at the federal headquarters of this party with Zapatero.
The head of the Executive has justified the offer to the former minister because "it is important to have the best" in political life and Bono "is among the best."
In addition, he has pointed out that "yes it seems" that the Manchego politician will be the candidate of the socialist group to preside over Congress if the socialists win in the upcoming elections.
Bono would replace Manuel Marín as president of the congress, who published on November 15 his decision not to run for the upcoming general elections and to abandon his career in active politics to dedicate himself to combating climate change at the university.
The former minister has acknowledged that the president of the government has not stopped insisting that he return to the political vanguard since leaving it two years ago.
In addition, he has pointed out that, just as the citizens know who the economic vice president will be if the PSOE wins the elections, his party has wanted to announce who will preside over Congress, in an "an act of transparency."
If he reaches office, Bono hopes to turn the House into "the house of respect rather than insult or scream." and to make it "resemble more and more citizens."
"Sometimes unfortunately it seems that the only place in Madrid where you can't speak quietly and quietly is Congress, the president of the government was once interrupted in the Senate 26 times."
He has also had words of praise for his current president, Manuel Marín and "his good work" and he did not want to see himself already occupying his position so as not to fall into what, he has pointed out, his opponents could see as "prepotence."
Climatic propaganda
Since the anti-climate-changing movement subjugates both skeptics of its predictions and those who prioritize other political and social battles, it is obliged to show iron coherence.
And more a leader of the movement that is president of the government like Zapatero and believes that this struggle is more important than that of Islamist terrorism and even intends to sign a "new contract with the planet."
Such an approach obliges him to explain why his government's action, or inaction, has made a decisive contribution to Spain &apos; s leading the EU in non-compliance with Kyoto.
Those who are responsible for non-default, in which sectors it has taken place and why his Government, that of the contract with the planet, has not avoided it.
In addition, it is necessary to explain with the utmost clarity to the Spaniards the measures they are going to take to curb climate change.
What companies will be affected, what citizen habits will have to be changed, what individual and collective energy savings we will be obliged to do, what economic consequences it will have.
I mean, who's gonna be sacrificed and who's gonna pay to save the planet.
But there's not been and there won't be those explanations.
Precisely because it's about sacrificing and paying.
The measures against climate change, the real measures, are unpopular.
Exclusive, uncomfortable and menacing for the accounts of companies and individuals.
Even the penny of the gasoline suggested by the PSOE seemed so electorally dangerous to Zapatero that he has rushed to deny it.
In other words, it's all about saving the planet from nowhere, with pure propaganda, with empty slogans of every real consequence.
With stunning phrases, commissions, committees, protocols, new positions.
With contracts with the planet, this gentleman so useful for election campaigns that he neither speaks nor denounces nor demands, but adorns the rallies and inspires tenderness.
As long as it's limited to being a purely virtual contracting party and don't pretend we're cycling by bike or cooling with the fan.
Detained by the mayor and the head of the local police of Totana for an alleged plot of urban corruption
The Civil Guard has arrested the mayor of the Murcian town of Totana, the "popular" José Martínez Andreo, the head of the local police, the secretary of the City Council and a hotel entrepreneur for possible urban crimes, sources of the investigation have today reported.
The mayor was arrested at his home and has been transferred to the Consistory, in whose dependencies he is currently together with numerous agents, who have also gone to the Department of Urban Planning and the municipal management company of the Industrial Soil and Housing.
These three arrests are in addition to the six carried out last Monday in Galicia, Murcia and Madrid, in an operation related to the requalification of more than 2 million hectares of rustic land in urbanizable so that the Galician company Nuaria would build 4,000 houses, after the payment of illegal commissions during the last legislature.
In addition, two other persons were not arrested but are charged in the case file, conducted by Totana &apos; s Court No. 1.
The first six detainees have been brought before the courts today.
According to the sources, the former governor of Totana and now autonomous parliamentarian of the PP, Juan Morales, is being investigated.
In addition, the ex-wife, the owner of a real estate agency registered today in Totana, has been imputed, as well as the current girlfriend of the former regent, who resides in Murcia capital.
The director and owner of Grupo Nuaria, Vigo lawyer and businessman Manuel N.A., was arrested in Nigrán (Pontevedra), as well as Pablo José M.G., Director of Suelo de Inmonuar, an agency integrated in the aforementioned Group, and through which the bribes would have been made.
The investigation is carried out by the Urban Crimes Group of the Central Operational Unit (UCO) of the Civil Guard, whose agents, in addition to the arrests, carried out eleven searches, most of them in companies related to the detainees and located in Madrid, Vigo, Murcia, Pontevedra, Las Rozas (Madrid) and Totana.
A single person was then apprehended in Totana, in particular the owner of a well-known poultry product company in the region, who could have acted as an intermediary.
The Nuaria Group was in charge of developing what would be the largest residential complex in the Murcian municipality of Totana, which would involve the construction of more than 5,000 homes, a golf course and two hotels with "spa."
The company acquired in Totana 2.2 million square meters of land that were requalified and its project would mean doubling the population of the municipality, which has 25,000 inhabitants.
The Nuaria Group integrates companies such as Autesa and Inomonuar, dedicated to the real estate promotion; Conycase, which manages the Vigue carcasses of Coruña Streets, Venezuela and the Plaza de Fernando el Católico; Hogartel, dedicated to the direct marketing sector; Preconiza, focused on the promotion, sale and installation of construction elements.
