But that's a small expense for some of Russia's wealthy.
"It's capacity up to 18 passengers," says Dan Firer, a representative for Gulfstream.
"But no one asks for that model of so many seats because it's for family private flights or for presidents of a company."
Mr. Firer was in charge of the Gulfstream cockpit last Friday at the Millionaire Fair, a four-day orgy of consumption held at an event center in the vicinity of the capital.
