It was the day before Thanksgiving when Ronald Livingston glanced through the "A Little Hit Healthy" restaurant window and watched as an ambulance climbed through White Cape Cod, two doors down on West Scott Avenue.
Suddenly, a cop's patrol car showed up.
And then another.
"Then I saw the ambulance go upstairs," Mr. Livingston, the restaurant's supervisor, said Wednesday.
"That's when I knew someone had died".
Authorities learned that the dead woman was Olga Arroyo, 41, an acquaintance of the Newark Police Department director.
Investigators are now attempting to determine whether she died due to a procedure carried out by an unauthorised plastic surgeon, who is not yet identified by police, but who works at the 212 West Scott Avenue home.
Authorities still don't determine what caused Ms. Arroyo's death, but they're waiting for the toxicological test even though the results won't be available until a few for a few weeks. This will help solve the mysterious death that grunted the Newark cop's upper ranks.
